IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `psa93-types`
IMPORT `psa93-leavers`
IMPORT `psa93-transfers`

-- Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Leaver case` HAS
    `the leaver`                                        IS A `Leaver facts`
    `a transfer`                                        IS A MAYBE `Transfer facts`

DECLARE `Leaver position` HAS
    `entitled to short service benefit`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `latest age short service benefit is payable from`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `may elect a cash transfer sum or contribution refund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contribution refund`                               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `last day to apply for a transfer`                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `transfer right lost`                               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `trustees' last day to transfer`                    IS A MAYBE DATE
    `trustees must notify the Regulator`                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref ss 71, 95, 98, 99, 101AA, 101AB
@export default The position under the Pension Schemes Act 1993 (UK) for a member leaving an occupational scheme early: whether they are entitled to short service benefit and the latest age it must be payable from (s 71); whether they may instead elect a cash transfer sum or contribution refund, and the refund (ss 101AA-101AB); and for a transfer of a cash equivalent, the last day to apply (s 95(1A)), whether the right is lost (s 98), and the trustees' last day to carry it out (s 99). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Leaver case`  @desc The leaver facts and any transfer
GIVETH A `Leaver position`
`the leaver position for` c MEANS
    `Leaver position` WITH
        `entitled to short service benefit`             IS ssb
        `latest age short service benefit is payable from` IS IF ssb THEN JUST (`the latest age from which short service benefit is payable for` l) ELSE NOTHING
        `may elect a cash transfer sum or contribution refund` IS refundable
        `contribution refund`                           IS IF refundable THEN JUST (`the contribution refund for` l) ELSE NOTHING
        `last day to apply for a transfer`              IS
            CONSIDER c's `a transfer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN `the last day to apply for a transfer for` l `with` t
        `transfer right lost`                           IS
            CONSIDER c's `a transfer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the transfer right is lost for` l `with` t)
        `trustees' last day to transfer`                IS
            CONSIDER c's `a transfer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN `the trustees' last day to transfer for` t
        `trustees must notify the Regulator`            IS
            CONSIDER c's `a transfer`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the trustees must notify the Regulator for` t)
    WHERE
        l MEANS c's `the leaver`
        ssb MEANS `is entitled to short service benefit` l
        refundable MEANS `may elect a cash transfer sum or contribution refund` l
